{"id": 28, "ts": 1780474884.2611547, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I concur with Sarah\u2019s shift to Candidate\u202fC as the provisional recommendation.\u202fC\u2019s record shows 100\u202f% reliability, a proven ability to create a positive crew atmosphere, calmness in crises, rapid correct decision\u2011making, and solid technical competence (\u201cunderstands complicated technology\u201d). Those attributes directly satisfy the core safety\u2011critical criteria of reliability, stress resilience, decision quality, and technical competence.\nBy contrast, Candidate\u202fD, while strong on concentration, problem\u2011solving, and responsibility, is described as arrogant with relatively weak leadership and we have no evidence of crew\u2011cooperation or professional communication.\u202fCandidate\u202fA, despite strong leadership, anticipation of danger, and excellent spatial vision, lacks any observed data on operational reliability or crew collaboration and also shows weaknesses in accepting criticism and organization.\u202fCandidate\u202fB still carries concerns about communication tone and weak numeric memory, which affect crew interaction and attention to detail.\nGiven the current evidence, Candidate\u202fC remains the most balanced fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
